From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaynelarocque <shaynelarocque@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:51:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Authoritative movement

In enforce mode the simulated position is written to the player through
the same accepted-move path a client claim takes today (events, chunk
moves, fall damage, statistics), and the zero-input server travel is
skipped while the simulation owns the player's movement. The truth is
already collided, so its move skips the second collision pass, and the
branch's interim positions (the move, the snap to the target and back
to the start for PlayerMoveEvent) skip the waypoint updates: only the
final position runs them.

The simulation is also the only writer of the player's pose, swimming,
gliding and item-use state: the server's own per-tick recomputation of
them is skipped, and a change the server makes on purpose (a plugin, an
axe disabling a shield, a finished meal) is reported so it reaches the
client in a transaction.

